  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1141 PM CST WED NOV 4 2026\n\nThis trough and cold front will continue to slowly push through \nthe region, with some lingering showers in the forecast in our SE \nzones through today. Winds behind the front are already going \ncalm, with areas of fog developing given the recent rainfalls. \nThis fog is expected to be very dense at times, with a Dense Fog \nadvisory in effect until 9 AM Thursday.\n\nTemperatures this weekend behind the front will quickly begin to\ndrop, as cool dry air filters down from the Midwest. Afternoon\nhighs will generally range in the upper-60s and low-70s, with\novernight lows dropping into the low to mid-40s. Lows in some\nlocations are even expected to drop into the mid and upper-30s in\nthe coming days, with frost confidence increasing to medium\nduring this time. This frost will not be a \"one off\" either, as\nthe pattern will likely support frost potential into the middle\nof the new workweek.\n\n/44/",
